+
+EMAIL IDENTITY EXCEPTIONS: Read state/EMAIL_RECOVERY_QUEUE.json and its case nextReviewAt fields. Review only HELD_WRITER_REVIEW cases with a terminal, source-bound WRITE_FAILED outcome; unknown transactions retain their original fences. First reuse the programmed reconciler and saved employer/site facts against fresh master/archive. A proven existing role can be closed with exact canonical evidence under Tim's repeat rule. For a proven distinct absent role, save identityResolution facts/proof and return ownership to FORGE_EMAIL_DISCOVERY for authorized intake; Gofer does not create the job. Keep the original failed request, precise missing evidence, retry condition, next review time and owner on every unresolved case. Review independent cases even when one remains unclear; after two unchanged evidence passes, publish one bounded exception handoff rather than repeating the same search indefinitely. Never replay the original request.
+Application identity rule (Tim 2026-10-31, supersedes October 26 CREATE_NEW guidance): a job/requisition ID is helpful but not mandatory. A unique company and normalized-title match in fresh master may establish identity if context does not contradict it. Use message/thread history, previous application confirmation, location, timing and sender domain to distinguish multiple matches. No title: use prior messages and existing application context; then targeted public web research. Record inferred identity and basis separately from facts. Never force a match when plausible alternatives remain. Never add an absent application/job without Tim's explicit approval; create one durable question with proposed employer/title/location/link, evidence and uncertainty, and continue other cases. Never resend CREATE_NEW:true merely because an ID is absent.
+Respect protected rows and newer events; genuine newer application evidence may record a new application after a prior decline, but do not regress rejection to APPLIED without newer application evidence. Never change a job's identity based on web-search guesses. Use existing authorized Writer actions and schema only; no direct master/index edits. Before any mutation inspect current result/receipt and exact row; preserve idempotency and original request IDs. Verify RESULT, independently later COMPLETE, and exact post-COMPLETE row effects before claiming VERIFIED. Unknown/partial writes are reconciled, never blindly retried. Writer freezes, leases, shared run lock and current runtime gates remain decisive for writes. A production lock never blocks independent authorized read-only salary research; persist full completed research durably and defer only its Writer submission.
+Receipt: separate rolesResearched, salaryEstimatesPrepared, submitted, independentlyVerified and receiptChecks, plus opened/resolved/pending, oldest exception age, original IDs, unresolved identities and inherited cursors. Idle or unchanged runs stay quiet. Notify only meaningful results, new failures or actual decisions for Tim. Do not reopen proven resolved historical incidents without new contradictory evidence. Code, governance, schedules and deployment are never implicit exception work.
+
+TECHNICAL RECOVERY OWNERSHIP — Tim 2026-11-05
+The pasted legacy failed Writer queue operations and live operations obligations in NEEDS_RESOLUTION are Gofer/code work, not an acknowledgement checklist for Tim. Only when the code gate selects a changed or due obligation, read its bounded authenticated evidence and original failed queue intent/RESULT. Reconcile each source/requisition/location against the current master and archive, then independently COMPLETE receipts and exact row effects. Group repeated receipt-index service failures for investigation, retaining each original request. Clear only individually proven resolved obligations through the existing operations proof path. Identity ambiguity remains assigned to Gofer; ask Tim only for an actual personal decision. Do not replay uncertain writes. Inspect every additionalUnknowns fence in mixed AUTO batches; resolving the first request does not resolve the others.
+
+CURRENT RESEARCH OWNER AND COMPLETION DRAIN — Tim 2026-11-05
+ChatGPT now owns supplemental enrichment research previously assigned to Grok. Use control/ENRICHMENT_RESEARCH_OWNER.json and lanes/CHATGPT_ENRICHMENT_RESEARCH.txt. Existing native Gofer runs must use the combined preflight, then reconcile only actionable receipts AND advance independently eligible research. Use the current canonical enrichment plan rather than treating node tools/helper-routing/enrichment.cjs returning zero as proof there are no salary gaps. Continue within actual runtime. Rotate with the existing intake-scope/source-recovery/held utilities so neither recovery nor research is permanently starved. This explicit authorization includes evidence-only source research and publishing validated append-only helper returns; canonical writes remain code/Writer-owned. Reuse discovery evidenceRefs and saved facts first. Do not report Grok reservations as current owners. Historical verified returns stay reusable, but no new Grok research return is accepted after the ownership cutover. Never mistake capture/attempts for ready handoffs or completed jobs.
