+Use tools/source-trial/job-identity.js and tools/source-trial/IDENTITY.md. Strong identity is a job-identity URL, employer-scoped requisition, scoped ATS posting ID, or compatible claimed PRIMARY_ID. Otherwise require a unique normalized employer/title/precise city-and-state match. Common abbreviations, neutral trailing company suffixes and state/country formatting may normalize; meaningful seniority, employer divisions and shifts remain distinct. Known requisition, employer, title or worksite conflicts and multiple canonical IDs remain ambiguous. Preserve identity-bearing query parameters and ATS board scope. Different LinkedIn/Indeed listing IDs need shared employer requisition/ATS evidence, not names/site alone. Pay comparables/review URLs are not job identity.
+Missing, remote, regional, national/global, multi-site or otherwise imprecise worksite evidence cannot establish a weak match or independent job. Different clear sites are not duplicates solely because employer/title match. An unresolved request fences its own posting/requisition and compatible site; the shared matcher permits a generic-title fence exception only for precise different-state single sites with no shared strong identity or broad scope. Same-state/metro/unknown sites and legacy incomplete fences stay protected. Never invent a requisition from an aggregator listing ID.
