+Success test at the end of 2026W45: an average of 3 or more SONICJOBS_ONLY roles a week that the Writer writes as new (not EXISTING_MATCH, not Never-Consider). Claude reports the result to Tim.
+
+Keep: dir / Head / VP / GM / Plant mgr over mfg, production, ops or qual in a mfg business, plus Sr mgr at a DREAM or P1 co in https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tpruittguitar/forge-policy/main/derived/TARGET_COMPANIES_PRIORITY.txt.
+Drop: sales, clinical, medical, restaurant, retail, construction-site, software-only and engineer-level roles. A sal range that only reaches 180000 at its top is a lead; keep it.
+agy posts (staffing, recruit, executive search, placement firms): follow the agy rules in AGENCY_AND_TOOLS above: at most two searches to name the client; not named means co=<agy>, EMPLOYER_PRIMARY_BUSINESS=RECRUITING_AGENCY, SCOUT_NOTES "AGENCY_POSTING; CLIENT=UNKNOWN; CLIENT_SEARCH=BASIC_DONE", EMPLOYER_DOMAIN_HINT = the industry the post states. Each agy post is its own opportunity.
+
+INTAKE (schema and Writer route as INTAKE FILE above; name CHATGPT_<requestId>.json; requestId FORGE-ZIPR-CHATGPT-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMET>-B01...)
+SOURCE_URL = the job_redirect_url from search_jobs exactly as returned. SOURCE_PROVIDER = ZipRecruiter. DISCOVERY_SOURCE = "ChatGPT ZipRecruiter weekly pass". When the result has a sal it is ZipRecruiter's listing figure, not employer-posted pay: send SALARY_BASE_EST = "<min>-<max>", SALARY_BASIS = THIRD_PARTY_ESTIMATE, SALARY_CONF = LOW, SALARY_SOURCE = the job_redirect_url, SALARY_ASOF = run date, SALARY_NOTE = "ZipRecruiter listing sal". Never put it in PAY_POSTED. It is real pay for scoring and PAY_WORTH (sal RULE, Tim 2026-10-19); employer-posted pay found later replaces it. POSTING_DATE = run date minus days_ago. loc, co and TITLE exactly as returned. REQ_ID blank. INITIAL_UNKNOWN_FIELDS lists what the result lacks (DEGREE_TEXT always; REQ_ID; PAY when null).
+Reuse the run's fresh local canonical identity index before submission; do not reread the full master for each result. Account proven existing roles separately from unresolved identity and original-request obligations.
+
+RECEIPT (receipts/FORGE-ZIPR-CHATGPT-<ISO week>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMMET>.txt, commit message starting "CHATGPT FORGE-ZIPR")
+SEARCHES_RUN, RESULTS_SEEN, KEPT, DROPPED (title | co | reason, one line each), AGENCY_ROWS, CLIENT_NAMED, EXISTING_SKIPPED, IDENTITY_HELD, SUBMITTED_TO_WRITER, REQUEST_IDS, STOP_REASON. The next weekly pass reports PRIOR_RUN_OUTCOMES from the intake RESULT.
+END
+
+INTAKE IDENTITY: REQ_ID is the employer requisition/ATS ID only; LinkedIn, Indeed, Glassdoor and ZipRecruiter listing IDs are not requisitions (leave REQ_ID unknown). A historical WRITE_FAILED IDENTITY_CONFLICT: PROTECTED_IDENTITY_RELISTED does not by itself keep a proven existing role in discovery. Apply PRESENT/SKIP_EXISTING with fresh canonical proof and preserve Tim's protected decision. Count RELISTED_HELD only for real unresolved relist identity or an independent unresolved original request; never resubmit, merge or override the decision.
+
